# Vauxhall Cavalier Mk1 four-door saloon, 1975-1981.
#
# The first Cavalier: General Motors' U-car, the Vauxhall version of the Opel
# Ascona B with a longer bonnet and Wayne Cherry's droop-snoot nose and
# rectangular headlamps. Launched September 1975, imported from Antwerp until
# Luton production began on 26 August 1977; replaced by the front-wheel-drive
# Mk2 in August 1981. Total production 238,980.
# https://www.aronline.co.uk/cars/vauxhall/cavalier/mk1/
# http://www.cavalierandchevetteclub.com/cavalier%20mk1%20saloon.htm
#
# Dimensions: 4,260 x 1,660 x 1,365 mm, wheelbase about 2,520 mm.
# https://www.classiccarreviews.co.uk/review/vauxhall/cavalier-mk1/saloon-1975-1981/
#
# Colours: Signal Yellow, Signal Red, Polar White and Regatta Blue are factory
# Vauxhall colours of the period (1976 Cavalier chart and the 1977-87 blue
# range). The reference photograph is a Signal Yellow 1978 car.
# https://www.uniquecarsandparts.net.au/colour_swatch_vauxhall_1970
# https://vauxhalltouchuppaint.com/vauxhall-cavalier-paint-codes/blue
#
# Colour shares and weight: the Cavalier sold at roughly a quarter to a third of
# Cortina volume in the late 1970s, so it is set at 180 against the Cortina's 500
# anchor, split by the measured 1970s share order: blue 65, red 50, white 40,
# yellow 25. Provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 150 km/h: a game-balance figure for the 1.6/1.9/2.0 range.
# Comfort 85/458: a mid-1970s family saloon, below the Sierra's 120/510 and above
# the Escort; the line gives 307.5, rounded to 310.
#
# Dates describe when the car was seen regularly on UK roads: launch September
# 1975, with a staggered 12-15 year tail by colour.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-cavalier-mk1.blend in the blends
# repository. References: citycars/references/vauxhall-cavalier-mk1/ (gitignored).
# Image credits: 1978 Cavalier, Charles01, CC BY-SA 3.0; Brecon Cavalier,
# Charles01, CC BY-SA 3.0, via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=VauxhallCavalierMk1(RegattaBlue)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=65
